{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You were admitted for nausea and vomiting again, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started right after I got home last time. I can’t keep anything down, not even water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you have your J-tube, correct? Have you been able to use it for feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I tried, but even the tube feeds make me nauseous. It’s been really hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you’re going through this again. We’ll start with IV fluids and some medications to help with the nausea and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. The only thing that helps is the lorazepam and morphine, like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve noted that from your history. We’ll give you IV lorazepam and morphine, since that’s what’s worked before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-04-28 14:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I just need something to break the cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-04-28 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling now? It’s been about two hours since your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-04-28 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. The nausea isn’t as intense, but my stomach still feels off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-04-28 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good start. Your labs came back — your potassium is a bit low at 3.4, and your bicarbonate was 20, which suggests mild acidosis, likely from vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-04-28 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-04-28 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s expected with dehydration from vomiting. We’re giving you fluids and will replace the potassium. It should correct over the next day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-04-28 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did a quick X-ray with contrast to confirm your J-tube is in the right place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the tube is positioned correctly, and there are no signs of complications. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I was worried it might have moved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start slowly increasing your tube feeds today. We want to make sure your stomach can tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I try sipping water too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-04-29 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s hold off on oral intake for now. We’ll focus on the tube feeds and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-04-30 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat labs look much better. Potassium is now 4.0, and bicarbonate is 25 — completely normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-04-30 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. I’m feeling less shaky too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-04-30 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lactate also came down from 2.1 to 0.9, which means your body is no longer under stress from dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-04-30 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that was from not keeping fluids down?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-04-30 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. When you vomit a lot, your body can’t maintain circulation well, but you’re back on track now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-04-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try a little apple juice through the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-04-30 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can add some clear liquids through the tube, yes. Let’s start with half-strength and see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-05-01 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well overnight — no nausea, and you kept all the feeds down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-05-01 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I actually feel hungry for the first time in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-05-01 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great sign. We’ll switch you to your full tube feeding formula today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-05-01 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And can I stop the IV meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-05-01 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, since you’re not having pain or nausea, we’ll discontinue the IV medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling really good. Do you think I can go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the plan. But we want to make sure you’re stable and have a plan for managing flares at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to keep coming back to the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We discussed this with your GI team. Since you’ve had three hospitalizations this month, we’re going to send you home with morphine and lorazepam tablets."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I can’t swallow them when I’m nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You can crush them and put them through your J-tube. That way, you can treat symptoms early at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That could really help. I wish we’d tried this sooner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also keep your other meds — levothyroxine, citalopram, omeprazole — going through the tube as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my vitamin D?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-05-01 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue that twice a month as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-05-01 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I walked down the hall twice today. I’m feeling stronger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-05-01 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. Your exam shows your abdomen is soft and not tender anymore, and your bowel sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-05-01 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m really ready to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-05-01 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you continue to do well overnight, we’ll discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel like a new person."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Remember to use the crushed lorazepam and morphine through your tube if nausea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I have my follow-up with Dr. ___ next week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and another appointment with your other GI doctor. They’ll help manage your gastroparesis long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to keep those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re going home with services to help with your care. Someone will check in with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. I live alone, so that helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care of yourself, and don’t hesitate to call your doctor or come back if symptoms worsen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-05-02 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-05-02 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just waiting for the discharge papers. I’m so ready to be home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-05-02 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring them shortly. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve packed everything. Can I ask one more thing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "If I use the meds at home and feel better, should I still call my GI doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please. Even if you improve, we want them to know what happened and adjust your plan if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll call right after I get home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and we hope not to see you back here soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-05-02 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same here. Thank you again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-04-28 14:40:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-05-02 16:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of gastroparesis and J-tube placement was readmitted one day after discharge due to a recurrent flare of nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. She was unable to tolerate oral intake or tube feeds initially. In the ED, she received IV fluids, lorazepam, and morphine, with improvement in symptoms. Admission labs showed mild hypokalemia and metabolic acidosis, both of which resolved with hydration. A contrast study confirmed proper J-tube placement without complications. Over the hospital stay, she gradually tolerated advancing tube feeds, discontinued IV medications, and resumed oral medications via the tube. Given her recent frequent hospitalizations, she was discharged with crushed lorazepam and morphine tablets to administer through her J-tube during future flares, along with follow-up appointments. She was ambulatory and stable at discharge.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Osteoporosis, unspecified",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Irritable bowel syndrome",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Other postprocedural status"
    ]
  }
}
